\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline Limitation: precision is a lower bound, not an exact figure.}{58}{paragraph*.124}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline A second, distinct bias: active-learning sampling skews which relevant companies get verified, not just how many.}{58}{paragraph*.126}%
\contentsline {paragraph}{\nonumberline A third bias, harder to quantify: the author personally breaks judge disagreements, then those decisions score the author's own system.}{59}{paragraph*.128}%
